<div class="publications">
  {%- comment -%}
    jekyll-scholar 7.2 only recognises the switches listed in its own optparse
    (see lib/jekyll/scholar/utilities.rb). An unknown switch such as --sort_by is
    split into a bare "--", which OptionParser reads as "end of options" and
    silently drops everything after it — which is why --group_by never applied.
    Keep this to real switches only.

    Order does NOT come from the order of entries in selected.bib. jekyll-scholar
    applies the global scholar.sort_by from _config.yml ("year, title", descending
    then ascending), so these five are the first five after that sort: newest year
    first, then alphabetical by title within the year. Adding an entry can push
    another one off the end.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% bibliography --file selected --group_by none --max 5 %}
</div>
